# Anthropic-family dispatch substrate

**House rule (operator 2026-07-17 / 2026-07-18):** substrate choice for Anthropic-family work — not a “how to spend API credits” guide.

## Defaults (binding)

| Path | Default |
|---|---|
| `model=anthropic/*` on `team_dispatch` / Stargate Anthropic Messages API | **PROHIBITED** |
| `model=cursor/*` on `seat=cursor-sdk` | **PERMITTED** except **Fable** |
| Anthropic-family consult (Opus / Sonnet / web-anthropic product) | **web-anthropic-cdp preferred** — corpus must be **cortex-packaged** (`cortex://`; ¬ rely on `workspaces://` / GitHub browse) |
| Codebase must be navigable on the executor | **`cursor/claude-opus-*`** (cursor-sdk) is acceptable |

**Fable:** CDP / web-anthropic product picker only — ¬ `anthropic/claude-fable-*` API and ¬ `cursor/*` Fable as standing default.

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| “Opus High” → `role=artisan model=anthropic/claude-opus-4-8` + `cost_intent` | CDP sealed ask **or** `seat=cursor-sdk model=cursor/claude-opus-4-8` |
| Self-attest `deliberate_high_cost` to unlock API Opus | Treat API as **off** unless operator **explicitly** overrides the house rule for that call |
| Cancel / re-route without operator bind when substrate was wrong | Ask substrate; ¬ silent cancel of a live dispatch |

## Stargate gate (residual mechanics — not the house rule)

Stargate still hard-gates explicit `model=anthropic/*` via `anthropic_override_gate` (`cost_intent=deliberate_high_cost` + reason, in-family profile, or review-child spawn). **Passing that gate ≠ house-rule permission.** Fleet default remains: do not select `anthropic/*`. Operator override of the house rule is a spoken/written exception for that dispatch — not routine self-attestation.

